==Trivia==
*The first use of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mortar_(weapon) mortars in warfare] was in 1413, where the Koreans used the ''wan'gu'' (gourd-shaped mortar) during a naval battle. Mortars are still used in modern warfare to this day as indirect fire weapons for close fire support.
*The Mortar's Evolution might be based off of an April Fools joke, where on 1/4/2016, certain Content Creators were given a different version of the game, with a Mortar that attacked by shooting [[Goblin Barrel|Goblin Barrels]] instead of boulders.
*The Mortar is 1 of 6 evolved [[cards]] associated with [[Goblins]], with the others being [[Dart Goblin/Evolution|Dart Goblin]], [[Goblin Cage/Evolution|Goblin Cage]], [[Goblin Giant/Evolution|Goblin Giant]], [[Goblin Barrel/Evolution|Goblin Barrel]], and [[Goblin Drill/Evolution|Goblin Drill]].
*The Mortar was the first [[:Category:Building Cards|building]] to receive a [[Card Evolution]].
*In the Korean and German language settings of the game, the Mortar's name translates to "Mine Thrower".
*Due to a glitch, the [[Tesla/Evolution|Evolved Tesla]] plays the Evolved Mortar's deployment sound when played by the opponent.
*The Mortar is unavailable in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]]. More specifically:
**It is 1 of 20 cards that is unavailable in [[Mirror]] mode, the others being [[Minions]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Cannon]], [[Tesla]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Tombstone]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Inferno Tower]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Elixir Collector]], [[Freeze]], [[Clone]], [[X-Bow]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Mighty Miner]], and the [[Monk]].
**It is unavailable in [[Global Spell|The Floor is Healing]] sub-[[:Category:Modes|mode]] of the Global Spell game mode, much like other building cards, as well as the [[Cannon Cart]].
*The Mortar's Evolution is the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].
*On 3/1/2024, the Evolved Mortar was supposed to receive a Goblin first attack time interval increase to 0.5 seconds (from 0.4 seconds), but this change [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-55-balance-wip was pulled back last minute].

